Part - 01

Day 22 Notes – Backend Setup (Node + Express)

1.Create Backend Folder
mkdir backend
cd backend

2.Initialize Project
npm init -y

3.Install Packages
npm install express cors

4.Basic Server Code (index.js)
import express from "express";
import cors from "cors";

const app = express();
const PORT = 5000;

app.use(cors());
app.use(express.json());

app.get("/", (req, res) => {
res.json({ message: "Backend is running" });
});

app.listen(PORT, () => {
console.log(Server running on http://localhost:${PORT});
});

5.Run the Server
node index.js

6.Important Points:
-express → creates the server
-cors → allows frontend to talk to backend
-express.json() → allows backend to read JSON data
-app.get() → creates a GET route
-app.listen() → starts the server

Key Point:
Backend runs on a different port (usually 5000) than React (5173).

