DAY 22 — NMAP (QUICK NOTES)

Nmap = Network Mapper → used for host discovery, port scanning, service enumeration, OS detection and NSE-based enumeration.

BASIC COMMANDS
nmap <TARGET> → scans default 1,000 common ports
nmap -p- <TARGET> → scans all 65,535 TCP ports
nmap -p 22,80,443 <TARGET> → specific ports
nmap -sn <NETWORK/CIDR> → host discovery only

SCAN TYPES
-sS → TCP SYN scan
-sT → TCP Connect scan
-sU → UDP scan

ENUMERATION
-sV → service/version detection
-sC → default NSE scripts
-O → OS detection
-A → OS + version + default scripts + traceroute

NSE
NSE = Nmap Scripting Engine
Used for discovery, enumeration and security checks.
Always understand a script before running it.

OUTPUT
-oN scan.txt → normal output
-oX scan.xml → XML
-oA scan → saves multiple formats

PENTEST WORKFLOW
Discover hosts
→ Find open ports
→ Identify services/versions
→ Run relevant NSE
→ Identify attack surface
→ Investigate interesting services
→ Save evidence

IMPORTANT
Open port ≠ vulnerability.
Service/version information tells you what to investigate next.
Only scan authorized targets/labs.
